Icarust reference and bundled assets
-----------------------------------

Moleflow was developed with LooseLab/Icarust as a reference for its MinKNOW
simulator design and implementation, not as a behavior-preserving port.
We thank the Icarust authors and contributors for their work.
https://github.com/LooseLab/Icarust
Reference revision: ef055864183ca2f149b748d29c34fe4ec1e74cac

The included Icarust assets retain MPL-2.0 licensing:
- models/r10_dna.tsv: unmodified copy of
  static/dna_r10.4.1_e8.2_400bps/R10_model.tsv.
- models/adapter.i16: little-endian int16 representation of
  static/prefix.squiggle.npy.

The model file is byte-identical to the referenced version; all 913 adapter
sample values are preserved. Signal noise, sampling, read-length distributions
and pore scheduling differ between the projects. Shared assets do not imply
identical simulated reads or equivalent Read Until behavior. Cross-project
output equivalence has not been validated.

The source repository is the provenance of these research assets. No claim is
made that they reproduce a current commercial pore model.

Crystal dependencies
--------------------

MIT-licensed dependencies: kojix2/grpc, kojix2/proto, kojix2/minknow,
kojix2/pod5.cr, and crystal-ameba/ameba (development only).
Resolved versions are recorded in shard.lock. Shards installs dependencies
under lib/; retain their original copyright and license notices.
proto declares MIT in lib/proto/shard.yml; the resolved revision does not
include a standalone LICENSE file.

MinKNOW protocol definitions and Google protobuf schemas carry additional
upstream notices. Retain the protocol notices alongside generated code and
the BSD license notices in lib/minknow/vendor/google/protobuf.

Native POD5 components
----------------------

The build downloads the official libpod5_format binary and builds the pod5.cr
compatibility library. POD5 C API sources and patches are MPL-2.0; Apache Arrow
headers are Apache-2.0 with bundled third-party notices; gsl-lite headers are
MIT-licensed. These licenses are not replaced by pod5.cr's MIT license.

See lib/pod5/THIRD_PARTY.md and lib/pod5/ext/LICENSE-POD5 after installation.
The native installation retains component licenses under
lib/pod5/vendor/pod5/licenses and compatibility sources under
lib/pod5/vendor/pod5/src/pod5-cr (or the configured POD5_NATIVE_PREFIX).
When redistributing native binaries, keep the applicable licenses and notices
and make the corresponding MPL-covered source available as required by MPL-2.0.

